  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 998940,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1986: Gangland Domination on the Commodore 64\n\nStep back into the gritty, lawless streets of 1920s Chicago in *1986*, a thrilling crime simulation for the Commodore 64. During Prohibition, fear and corruption reign supreme as gangs battle for control of the city's underworld. You begin as a newly released convict, a nobody struggling to survive in a world of blackmail, robberies, and readily available firearms. Your goal: to rise through the ranks and claim the coveted Mafia Throne.\n\nGameplay revolves around completing increasingly dangerous and morally questionable odd jobs – from petty theft to more serious offenses – to earn money and build your reputation. Acquire a car, arm yourself, secure a safe haven, and ultimately assemble your own loyal gang. \n\n*1986* boasts a unique visual style, utilizing PETSCI graphics with a modified character set, complemented by vibrant, comic-book style images depicting key locations and events. While the sound is minimal, the game's atmosphere and challenging gameplay create an immersive and engaging experience, offering a taste of the dangerous life of a Chicago gangster."
    },
